  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">DETERRING WILDLIFE CRIME AND ILLEGAL WILDLIFE TRAFFICKING OF RHINOCEROS AND TIGER BODY PARTS IN THE TRANSBOUNDARY EASTERN HIMALAYAS</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">THE SERVICE HEREBY INCORPORATES THE RECIPIENTS APPLICATION SUBMITTED TO AND APPROVED BY THE SERVICE INTO THESE AWARD TERMS AND CONDITIONS.THE OVERALL GOAL OF THIS PROJECT IS TO CHECK AND REDUCE WILDLIFE CRIME AND ILLEGAL WILDLIFE TRADE OF RHINOCEROS AND TIGER BY 2024.THE PROJECT OBJECTIVES ARE AS FOLLOWS: (1) INCREASE EFFECTIVENESS OF LAW ENFORCEMENT AGENCIES BY STRENGTHENING THEIR TOOLS, AND CAPACITY TO CHECK AND REDUCE WILDLIFE CRIME AND ILLEGAL WILDLIFE TRADE OF RHINO AND TIGERS BY 2024 (2) GENERATE, COLLATE, AND SHARE INFORMATION ON ILLEGAL WILDLIFE TRADE HOTSPOTS AND PATHWAYS IN THE EASTERN HIMALAYAS WITH RELEVANT LAW ENFORCEMENT AGENCIES TO TRIGGER NEEDED LEGAL ACTION TO CURB WILDLIFE CRIME ON RHINO AND TIGER BODY PARTS AND OTHER THREATENED WILDLIFE (3) ESTABLISH A COMMUNITY-BASED SURVEILLANCE, MONITORING AND WILDLIFE CRIME PREVENTION SYSTEM IN COLLABORATION WITH LAW ENFORCEMENT AGENCIES IN ASSAM, ARUNACHAL PRADESH AND MANIPUR, TO REDUCE THE SITE LEVEL ILLEGAL WILDLIFE OFFENCES TARGETING RHINOS, TIGERS AND OTHER THREATENED ANIMALS BY 2024 AND (4) ESTABLISH TWO NOVEL TRANSBOUNDARY COLLABORATIONS TO REDUCE TRANSNATIONAL ORGANIZED CRIME ON RHINOCEROS, TIGERS AND OTHER KEY SPECIES.</narrative>
  </description>
